secondaryOutcomes.description:
Occurrence of post-operative CSA-AKI was using modified KDIGO criteria within 7 days after CPB: An increase in sCr by ≥0.3 mg/dL in a 48-hour period or ≥1.5\*baseline within the 7 days following CPB.

Stages of post-CSA-AKI kidney function to determine AKI progression:

* Post-AKI stage 0 - Complete recovery: sCr \<1.1\*baseline or partial recovery: sCr ≥1.1 to \<1.5 × baseline;
* Post-AKI Stage 1 - sCr ≥1.5 to \<2.0\*baseline;
* Post-AKI Stage 2 - sCr ≥2.0 - \<3.0\*baseline;
* Post-AKI Stage 3 - sCr ≥3.0\*baseline, or sCr ≥4.0 mg/dL in participants meeting CSA-AKI criteria or KRT.

AKI progression:

* AKI recovery - Complete: sCr \<1.1\*baseline or Partial: sCr ≥1.1 - \<1.5\*baseline
* AKI improvement - Move down 1 or more stages from the highest CSA-AKI stage, or remained in stage 3 but discontinued KRT;
* Stable AKI - Unchanged AKI or KRT status;
* Worsening AKI - Moved up 1 or more stages from the highest CSA-AKI stage, or Remained in Stage 3 but initiated KRT.

